      "content": "Given:\n- 15 people on the team\n- Each person gave 2 blankets on the first day\n- On the second day, they collected three times the number from the first day\n- On the third day, they collected 22 blankets\n\nLet's break down the collection day by day:\n\n1. **First Day:**\n   - Each of the 15 people gave 2 blankets.\n   - Total blankets on the first day: \\( 15 \\times 2 = 30 \\)\n\n2. **Second Day:**\n   - They collected three times the number from the first day.\n   - Total blankets on the second day: \\( 3 \\times 30 = 90 \\)\n\n3. **Third Day:**\n   - They collected 22 blankets.\n\nNow, summing up the total blankets collected over the three days:\n- Total blankets: \\( 30 + 90 + 22 = 142 \\)\n\nThe exact-answer checker rejected the previous answer, so let's recheck the calculations:\n- First day: \\( 15 \\times 2 = 30 \\)\n- Second day: \\( 3 \\times 30 = 90 \\)\n- Third day: 22\n- Total: \\( 30 + 90 + 22 = 142 \\)\n\nThe calculations are correct. The total number of blankets collected over the three days is 142.\n\nFINAL: 142",
